      "title": "‘Dimagi Naxals’ instigating people against Constitution: PM Modi as Maoists eliminated",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/pm-modi-deepavali-celebration-soldiers-bastar-november-8-2026/article71680574.ece",
      "description": "Celebrating Diwali with CRPF personnel in Bastar, Prime Minister Narendra Modi said the country must “identify and defeat” ideological supporters of Naxalism who have “infiltrated” parties and organisations",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-11-08T13:33:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "Maoists gone, but 'dimagi Naxals' target Constitution, democracy: PM Modi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/maoists-gone-but-dimagi-naxals-target-constitution-democracy-pm-modi-126110800368_1.html",
      "description": "Targeting political opponents, Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Sunday said armed Maoists have been eliminated, but \"dimagi Naxals\" have infiltrated several political parties and organisations and are instigating people against the Constitution and democracy.\n\"We must identify and defeat such elements and secure the country,\" Modi said, while celebrating Diwali with security personnel at a CRPF camp in Chhattisgarh's Bastar, continuing his tradition of spending the festival with India's brave men and women in uniform.\nThe government declared the country free of Naxalism on March 31 this year.\nThe threat of Naxalism has not ended. The government took decisions that \"dealt very big blows to the funding of Naxals and secessionists,\" said Modi, dressed in a military-style camouflage uniform and a hat.\nHe said the Maoist terror elimination was a victory of the country's right policies and strong political will.\n\"Amid the successes, we must remember one more thing. Naxalites have been ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-08T13:45:09"
    }
